# 14 October 2026: the method sheet of the rhythm module, as code. Every method is run through the SAME four phases and is
# scored after each of them against the same truth, so two methods are compared on their principle and nothing else:
#   P1 signal      a number per picture boundary from the method's principle (scored: area under the ROC curve of true cuts
#                  against every other boundary, traps included);
#   P2 candidates  adaptive or global peak picking on that signal (scored: F1 at +-1 frame);
#   P3 verify      persistence, flash return and isolation (scored: F1 at +-1 frame);
#   P4 place       exact frame, transitions by their middle (scored: F1 at 0 frame and +-1 frame).
# Thresholds of P2 are tuned per method on the TRAIN videos only; the sheet reports TEST videos separately.
# FR : la feuille de methodes en code : memes quatre phases pour chaque methode, meme verite, seuils regles sur l'entrainement.
